^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
from_integer built a floating-point constant whose type had lost the
#c_type comment, so the value 0.0 of double() had a type that was neither
double nor long double and every overload needed a conversion.  libc++
19's __promote (`decltype((__test(_Args()) + ...))') then deduced no
type, and std::__hermite in <cmath> lost its body (macOS CI job).
